{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah","id":1532146,"title":"Bloodlines 2 - Clan Highlight Brujah","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-07T03:37:21-08:00","id":1532146,"title":"Bloodlines 2 - Clan Highlight Brujah","content":"The <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/clan-highlight-brujah\" target=\"_blank\">first highlight for the Clan Brujah in Bloodlines 2 has come out</a> and it not only shows off the Brujah abilities but also reveals more about how the ability-tree in the game works:<br /> <br /> Clan Brujah Abilities:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you choose your clan, you will start out with a passive ability unique to each clan. You are then able to unlock abilities from the Ability Tree, starting with your chosen clan. Each ability requires spending Ability Points to unlock, which are earned from completing missions, combat and exploration. At the peak of the Ability Tree, you can unlock the clan Perk, a reward to those dedicated enough to unlock all of the abilities for a clan, giving a permanent passive upgrade.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Brutality</b><b> (Clan Passive)</b><br /> <br /> After feeding, become flushed with vampiric strength, temporarily increasing the power of all your melee attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Taunt</b><br /> <br /> Use your supernatural Presence to enrage an opponent or civilian prey, compelling them to attack you. While enraged, the target takes increased damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Charge</b><br /> <br /> Surge forward with preternatural speed and rage, grabbing an enemy you collide with to use as a battering ram to knock down others in your path.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Strikes</b><br /> <br /> Target multiple opponents and unleash an unstoppable hail of punches, with the final strike dealing increased damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Earthshock</b><br /> <br /> Slam the ground with explosive force, flinging surrounding enemies into the air.<br /> <br /> <b>Pulverise</b><b> (Clan Perk)</b><br /> <br /> Killing enemies without feeding still activates your Clan Passive. </div> </div> </div><br /> All pretty self-explanatory. The previous Dev-diary mentioned the Taunt-ability would be useful for targeting enemies with shooting-attacks so that they would be forced to attack you in melee. I wonder how relevant that will be. Because if there are areas with a lot of enemies that shoot, a melee-heavy build like a Brujah-character could become quite annoying to play. Also, the Clan-perk isn't as good as it seems at first glance. We've seen from the gameplay-video that Abilities are on a cooldown-timer linked to charges you generate via feeding. So, for example, in the gameplay-video it took two charges (aka two feeding-actions) to activate the Charge-ability. So you still will use feeding in combat anyways.<br /> <br /> But I have far more opinions about what this reveal says about the ability-tree in Bloodlines 2:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Customizing your playstyle</b><br /> <br /> In Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2, you can play your character in different ways. Brujah are a more brawler type, and the abilities are focused around supporting that. We wanted to make sure that this is not an ability optimization game where you need to go through a multitude of abilities and weigh them against each other. Playing a clan should be straight forward if you want it to be.<br /> <br /> While this is true, you can also dive deeper into the customization of your playstyle. This is done by visiting important Seattle vampires that are sworn to assist the Sheriff (you) including offering their Blood to help unlock abilities from their clan. Abilities from other clans may cost more AP depending on how well they align with your clans Disciplines. The Brujah Disciplines are Celerity (speed enhancing abilities) Potence (strength enhancing abilities) and Presence (the supernatural ability to attract, awe, or terrify)) so if another clan has a speed enhancing ability it would cost less AP to unlock than an ability for a Discipline Brujah don\u2019t have, such as becoming stealthier which is part of the Obfuscate Discipline. Unlocking additional Clan Perks will make them stack, so you can collect them all if you wish, elevating your power much closer to elder level.<br /> <br /> While the activated abilities and Clan Perk can be learned from the other clans, your clan passive can not. This means that you can combine features from other clans in hundreds of different ways, but your Brujah playthrough will remain unique from playing as another clan who branches into Brujah abilities. </div> </div> </div>So, outside of the Clan-Passive and the Clan-Perk, every character has access to every Discipline. Now in that context, it has to be considered that the UI indicates that you can only ever equip four powers at the time. So while AP-costs for acquiring non-Clan-powers might differ, this is a model where the further you go into the game, the more the character-builds will start to look the same (depending on how generous the game is with AP, it might be possible to end up with all the Discipline-powers unlocked). I'm sure people will write game-guides and discuss which powers are good and which ones aren't worth buying. For example, in theory, this might lead to things like &quot;It's not worth unlocking Lightning Strikes, instead bank your AP and unlock the Tremere blood-dagger-shooting-ability instead.&quot;. What this certainly does is disincentivize repeated playthroughs. I guess, this also depends on how heavy the roleplaying-element in the game is and how much your Clan matters in that aspect. But gameplay-wise, outside from the Clan-passive and the Clan-perk (which don't seem too big of a deal when looking at the Brujah-example), over the course of the game you unlock whatever powers seem good and you mix and match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T04:30:28-08:00","id":1532149,"title":"","content":"Did anyone take a look at this wealth of options for Serious Thuggery and think \u201cHow hilarious would it be to roleplay Our Hero as a Philosopher-King, in-between acts of hand to hand brutalities?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T09:01:36-08:00","id":1532164,"title":"","content":"They really want to sell this as an action game to an audience that doesn't give a shit about action games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T12:03:57-08:00","id":1532178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah#post1532146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But gameplay-wise, outside from the Clan-passive and the Clan-perk (which don't seem too big of a deal when looking at the Brujah-example), over the course of the game you unlock whatever powers seem good and you mix and match.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it really depends on how the other trees are built and the wider action economy. If every Clan's passive activates on feeding, Pulverize should be interesting to go for to spice up replays as long as killing vs. feeding is a meaningful choice. If the Banu Haqim have a passive that gives them bonuses to stealth and sneak attacks after feeding, but feeding is long enough, and obvious enough comparing to just killing, stringing together stealth kills with Pulverize could be a pretty different experience from other options (though as noted, how generous the game is with points is going to matter to how same-y play throughs will feel).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:50:48-08:00","id":1532191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah?p=1532178#post1532178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it really depends on how the other trees are built and the wider action economy. If every Clan's passive activates on feeding, Pulverize should be interesting to go for to spice up replays as long as killing vs. feeding is a meaningful choice. If the Banu Haqim have a passive that gives them bonuses to stealth and sneak attacks after feeding, but feeding is long enough, and obvious enough comparing to just killing, stringing together stealth kills with Pulverize could be a pretty different experience from other options (though as noted, how generous the game is with points is going to matter to how same-y play throughs will feel).</div> </div> </div> </div>From the looks of it, the ability-trees are just a list of the powers for the four playable Clans with your chosen Clan adding the passive and the perk. As for killing vs. feeding, the way it looked in the gameplay-trailer when you trigger the feeding, you can't be interrupted. And I imagine everybody's gonna do the same kind of feeding as that's how the powers are activated and their usage is paced. And from the looks of it in the gameplay-trailer there are no stealth-kills but rather just the option to immediately feed on an enemy who hasn't seen you. Due to the scenario in the gameplay-trailer the killed enemies immediately disappeared but I assume they have a stealth-system of enemies reacting to killed enemies and there maybe being options for making corpses disappear... Well, at least I assume that's there but who knows... But in combat, you just have to get an enemy low, you press the two shoulder-buttons on your controller and the feeding happens. As for stealth, you have the telekinesis and the gliding anyway.<br /> <br /> The way I could see Pulverize being interesting is if, for example, it would take three light punches to kill a light enemy but with the Brujah Clan passive, it only takes one light punch and so with the perk it's easy to string together a bunch of melee-kills. But aside from the abilities, level-design will matter here as well. Depending on that, stealth might be better or or worse compared to just starting the combat and stringing together melee-kills and combat-feeding.<br /> <br /> Also, hopefully, the only reason this Clan-highlight didn't come with a gameplay-trailer was because we've already seen plenty of the Brujah-powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah?p=1532164#post1532164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They really want to sell this as an action game to an audience that doesn't give a shit about action games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully, the only reason we don't get to see the roleplaying-systems outside of combat is because they're still working on those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T14:20:41-08:00","id":1532195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah?p=1532164#post1532164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They really want to sell this as an action game to an audience that doesn't give a shit about action games.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's true that the game was almost canceled that would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T15:47:40-08:00","id":1532200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah?p=1532195#post1532195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's true that the game was almost canceled that would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand:<br /> <br /> 1. Hardsuit Labs promised a bunch of stuff to Paradox and Paradox bought it hook, line, and sinker.<br /> <br /> 2. Paradox even invested enough money to buy a huge chunk of Hardsuit Labs.<br /> <br /> 3. SOMETHING behind the scenes resulted in Hardsuit Labs firing Mitsoda and Avellone before dumping all of their writing that made up almost all of the side content.<br /> <br /> 4. They were also suddenly way way way behind on the game and no end in sight. Paradox felt cheated and lied to.<br /> <br /> 5. Paradox pulled the plug.<br /> <br /> 6. The Chinese Room said they could finish the game but wanted freedom to do it how they wanted.<br /> <br /> 7. Paradox said sure and demanded radio silence until they were close to finishing it.<br /> <br /> 8. TCR reused a bunch of assets but focused on a Camarilla-focused stealth and action game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T03:20:00-08:00","id":1532280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah?p=1532200#post1532200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 6. The Chinese Room said they could finish the game but wanted freedom to do it how they wanted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I would add here is that the rumor is the reason Paradox went with TCR was that they didn't just promise to finish the game but that they would do so <i>quickly</i>. And we've seen that in action, last Fall when the first previews came out, we saw footage from the game in its alpha-stage. Supposedly one year after that (so Q4 of this year), they will have released a finished game.<br /> <br /> Something like that brings to mind that stereotypical &quot;triangle of constraints&quot;: You can have it fast, you can have it good, you can have it cheap - pick two. Of course, reality often isn't that cut and dry. But I think this aspect of making the game quickly will be one of those things that nobody will talk about if the game is good and it will be mentioned <i>a lot</i> if the game is bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T09:28:24-08:00","id":1532291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532146-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-brujah?p=1532280#post1532280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I would add here is that the rumor is the reason Paradox went with TCR was that they didn't just promise to finish the game but that they would do so <i>quickly</i>. And we've seen that in action, last Fall when the first previews came out, we saw footage from the game in its alpha-stage. Supposedly one year after that (so Q4 of this year), they will have released a finished game.<br /> <br /> Something like that brings to mind that stereotypical &quot;triangle of constraints&quot;: You can have it fast, you can have it good, you can have it cheap - pick two. Of course, reality often isn't that cut and dry. But I think this aspect of making the game quickly will be one of those things that nobody will talk about if the game is good and it will be mentioned <i>a lot</i> if the game is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is it that they've had it for a few years. If they've been reusing assets, they haven't been doing it super-fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T10:02:40-08:00","i